From df4e773d4d031776cda6faba3c16b88196ed791e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jolyon Brown <jolyon@limilo.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 22:06:32 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 54/59] Fix double logical not folding to its operand

The parser applies ! through LogicInvertExpression, which removed an
inner ! by returning its operand: !!x became x.  That keeps the truth
value, all a condition needs, but !!x is a value, 0 or 1: !!5 was 5,
char c = !!(f & 0x100) was 0, and !!p kept the pointer's type, so
int r = !!p was rejected ("Cannot assign incompatible types").  The
inner ! now goes only when its operand is 0 or 1 already (a relational,
&&, || or ! expression), or is of class type: a class without an
operator! still reaches bool through its operator bool(), as before.
The previous commit folds ! of a constant, so !!1 stays a constant.

!!x now has the type ! gives, Oscar64's one-byte bool, so sizeof(!!x)
is 1 as sizeof(!x) already was; C would say sizeof(int).

It is nethack64's repro r52.  NetHack writes !! 98 times, such as
res = !!revive(obj); the integer ones compiled to the wrong value with
no diagnostic.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 oscar64/Declaration.cpp | 8 ++++++--
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/oscar64/Declaration.cpp b/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
index 60c9807..cdc4e54 100644
--- a/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
+++ b/oscar64/Declaration.cpp
@@ -452,9 +452,13 @@ bool Expression::IsSame(const Expression* exp) const
 	}
 }
 
-Expression* Expression::LogicInvertExpression(void) 
+Expression* Expression::LogicInvertExpression(void)
 {
-	if (mType == EX_LOGICAL_NOT)
+	// The built-in !!x is 0 or 1, so the inner ! can only go when its operand is 0 or 1
+	// already.  A class operand with no operator! is left to its conversion to bool.
+	if (mType == EX_LOGICAL_NOT && (mLeft->mType == EX_LOGICAL_NOT || mLeft->mType == EX_LOGICAL_AND ||
+		mLeft->mType == EX_LOGICAL_OR || mLeft->mType == EX_RELATIONAL ||
+		(mLeft->mDecType && mLeft->mDecType->IsStructOrUnion())))
 		return mLeft;
 	else if (mType == EX_LOGICAL_AND)
 	{
